            "review_title": "Review at Nu Cuoi Charity Restaurant",
            "review_text": "AhEkuEku\nSan Jose, California22 contributions\n0\nCan't find cheaper, better tasting food anywhere in HCMC\nDec 2014 • Solo\nNu Cuoi Charity Shop is a restaurant set up to feed people for a very reasonable price. Meal is set each day and there is no menu. You go in, pay 2000VND, yes, only 2000VND, and go in line to where they hand out the meal. There is always some type of meat or fish, vegetable, soup, banana, and all the rice you can eat. Seating is tight and the atmosphere is one of people that are there to eat, and not enjoy the ambiance. It is noisy, vibrant, and somewhat stressful, but the food is delicious. You won't be rushed by the staff, but with people waiting, you'll feel the need to eat and get up to go. It is lunch only, and they start serving at 11:00am. Normally, if you get there close to 12:30pm, there won't be much left. The restaurant is there to help serve the poor of Saigon, but the staff will never turn anyone away. Everyone is welcome. For 10 cents American, you can't go wrong.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 4, 2015",
